  "title": "Soundscapes",
  "html": "<div class=\"task note-list\"><h3>Questions 31–40</h3><p class=\"instructions\">Complete the notes. Write <strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong> for each answer.</p><h4 class=\"task-title\">Soundscapes</h4><div class=\"form-row section-heading\">Soundscape – the sound environment</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>the term was first used by a Canadian, Murray Schafer, a well-known <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"31\" id=\"q31\" name=\"q31\" placeholder=\"31\" aria-label=\"Question 31\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\"></div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>the soundscape is not just noise, but has <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"32\" id=\"q32\" name=\"q32\" placeholder=\"32\" aria-label=\"Question 32\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\">, which can be interpreted</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>divisions of the soundscape</div><div class=\"form-row indented\">– biophony – created by living organisms, e.g. <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"33\" id=\"q33\" name=\"q33\" placeholder=\"33\" aria-label=\"Question 33\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\"></div><div class=\"form-row indented\">– geophony – caused by non-biological forces, e.g. <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"34\" id=\"q34\" name=\"q34\" placeholder=\"34\" aria-label=\"Question 34\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\"></div><div class=\"form-row indented\">– anthrophony – made by humans</div><div class=\"form-row section-heading\">Conclusions of Bernie Krause</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>every sound in nature has a unique <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"35\" id=\"q35\" name=\"q35\" placeholder=\"35\" aria-label=\"Question 35\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\"></div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>the sounds of nature are harmonious in <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"36\" id=\"q36\" name=\"q36\" placeholder=\"36\" aria-label=\"Question 36\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\"> and frequency</div><div class=\"form-row section-heading\">Soundscape changes can be</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>an indication of a change in the <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"37\" id=\"q37\" name=\"q37\" placeholder=\"37\" aria-label=\"Question 37\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\"> of an environment</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>a warning of the presence of different types of <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"38\" id=\"q38\" name=\"q38\" placeholder=\"38\" aria-label=\"Question 38\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\">, e.g. insecticides</div><div class=\"form-row section-heading\">Equipment used in the study of soundscapes</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>acoustic recorders – data are used to create <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"39\" id=\"q39\" name=\"q39\" placeholder=\"39\" aria-label=\"Question 39\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\"> in 3-D</div><div class=\"form-row section-heading\">Most common query</div><div class=\"form-row indented\"><span class=\"bullet\">•</span>What is the noisiest creature?</div><div class=\"form-row indented\">Answer: probably a particular kind of <input class=\"gap choice-gap\" data-q=\"40\" id=\"q40\" name=\"q40\" placeholder=\"40\" aria-label=\"Question 40\" autocomplete=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" data-min-width=\"135\" style=\"--listening-gap-width:135px\">, which lives in the ocean</div></div>",
